@startuml
autonumber
participant "tick_scheduler" as loop
participant "run_market" as market
participant "latent_market" as noise
participant "the feed" as feed
participant "its process" as process
participant "market_board" as values
participant "NATS" as nats

loop -> loop : fire the series whose mark is reached\n(heat sampled, pace read, mark fixed when the gap was drawn)
loop -> market : driver source(series, at, out)
market -> noise : driver(series, from, to, out)
noise --> market : K standard normals, correlated by loading
market --> loop : how many it wrote
loop -> feed : body(tick_context{observed_at, elapsed, simulated, tail_tilt, drivers})
feed -> process : next_with_normal(driver) or next(elapsed)
process --> feed : the new price or state
feed -> values : publish_curve(id, ...) or publish_spot(id, ...)
feed -> nats : market_tick, and adapter_tick when it has an adapter
note over values : read on the loop, by id, no lock:\na curve and a spot for the pair, merged into one market
feed -> nats : one publish per point, as the run always did
@enduml
